# BBSFirewall - Management API IP allowlist
#
# Source IPs / CIDRs allowed to call the management API (the /api/* routes on
# the config editor's HTTPS port). This is OPTIONAL and independent of
# trustedhosts.txt: an API caller does NOT need to be a trusted editor host.
#
# One IP or CIDR per line. IPv4 and IPv6 both work. Lines starting with # are
# comments; an inline # comment after an entry is also allowed.
#
# IMPORTANT: unlike trustedhosts.txt, an EMPTY or MISSING file here does NOT
# lock anyone out — it means "any source IP may call the API". The API key
# (API_KEY in .env) is always required regardless. Add entries only to narrow
# access to known dashboard servers.
#
# Examples:
#   203.0.113.10           the dashboard server
#   198.51.100.0/24        a hosting range
#   2001:db8:abcd::/48     an IPv6 range
#
# To use this file:
# 1. Copy to api-trustedhosts.txt
# 2. Add the IPs / ranges your dashboard calls the API from
# 3. Set API_TRUSTEDHOSTS_PATH=./api-trustedhosts.txt in your .env (this is the default)

# 203.0.113.10
# 198.51.100.0/24
